      <div type="clause" n="2.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:WiLad">Wl lad</ref> 2.1</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-h">7 gif he untrum byð 7 nelle þæt ornest oððe ne mage, begyte him lahlicne spalan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-h">And if he is infirm and will not or cannot undertake trial by combat, he shall procure a lawful substitute.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="484"><ref target="clause:WlArt_6-1">Wl art 6.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Wl art. 6, [?]</note>
        <note type="comparisonIncomplete">Some of Liebermann’s notes here are cut off in the gutter of the scan used, and are still to be completed.</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:WlArt_6-1">Wl art 6.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 232–233 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
